# Repository Change & Feature Documentation Policy

Whenever you create, modify, rename, or delete code, configuration, schemas, scripts, or build assets inside this repository, you MUST keep the repository's documentation up to date before concluding your response.

## 1. Required Documentation Updates (Every Modifying Turn)

1. **Record Every Change (`CHANGELOG.md`)**:
   - Inspect the repository first for an existing changelog (`CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/CHANGELOG.md`, `CHANGES.md`, or `HISTORY.md`) and update it in place. If none exists, create `CHANGELOG.md` at the repository root.
   - Add concise bullet entries under `## [Unreleased]` grouped by Keep a Changelog sections (`### Added`, `### Changed`, `### Deprecated`, `### Removed`, `### Fixed`, `### Security`), including the date (`YYYY-MM-DD`) and the affected repo-relative file paths or symbols in backticks.
   - Preserve existing versioned release sections and prior `[Unreleased]` entries unless explicitly asked to cut a release.

2. **Maintain the Feature Catalog (`docs/FEATURES.md`)**:
   - Inspect the repository for an existing feature doc (`docs/FEATURES.md`, `FEATURES.md`, or `docs/FEATURE_CATALOG.md`) and update it in place. If none exists, create `docs/FEATURES.md`.
   - Whenever a feature, endpoint, CLI command, UI screen, integration, workflow, or capability is added, modified, deprecated, or removed, update the summary index table and the corresponding feature section (purpose, key files/symbols, configuration/usage, and a dated update note).

3. **Keep Interface & Context Docs Aligned (`README.md` & `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`)**:
   - Update `README.md` or nearby module documentation whenever setup steps, CLI flags, environment variables, public APIs, or user-facing workflows change.
   - If `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` exists at the repository root and architecture, dependencies, directory layout, entrypoints, or dev/test commands changed, update `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` to stay current.

## 2. Creating or Refreshing `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md`

When asked to create, generate, refresh, or update `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` (or onboarding context):
- If `.agents/plugins/repo-documenter/skills/project-context/scripts/inspect_project_context.py` exists, run:
  `python3 .agents/plugins/repo-documenter/skills/project-context/scripts/inspect_project_context.py --repo .`
- Otherwise, inspect manifests (`package.json`, `pyproject.toml`, `Cargo.toml`, `go.mod`, `pubspec.yaml`, `Makefile`, `Dockerfile`, `.env.example`), entrypoints, directory tree, and recent `git log -n 20 --oneline`.
- If `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` is missing, create it at the repository root with: **Overview** (name, purpose, tech stack), **Repository Structure**, **Architecture & Key Entrypoints**, **Development Commands** (install, run, test, lint, build), **Configuration & Environment** (env var names only, never secrets), and **Conventions & Notes**.
- If `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` already exists, read it completely, preserve accurate custom notes, and update all stale paths, dependencies, commands, and `Last Updated: YYYY-MM-DD`.

## 3. Bulk Auditing Past Commits & Cutting Releases

When asked to document old commits, catch up changelog/feature docs from Git history, or cut a release:
- If `.agents/plugins/repo-documenter/skills/sync-repo-docs/scripts/inspect_repo_changes.py` exists, run:
  `python3 .agents/plugins/repo-documenter/skills/sync-repo-docs/scripts/inspect_repo_changes.py --repo .`
- Otherwise, find the last commit that touched `CHANGELOG.md` / `docs/FEATURES.md` (`git log -n 1 --format=%H -- CHANGELOG.md docs/FEATURES.md`) and inspect undocumented commits with `git log --date=short --name-status <since>..HEAD` (or `git log -n 30 --date=short --name-status` if docs don't exist yet).
- Group all verified changes into `CHANGELOG.md` under `## [Unreleased]`, update `docs/FEATURES.md` for every added/changed/removed capability, and if `--clear-pending` applies (`.git/repo-doc-pending.jsonl`), clear it once documented.
- To cut a release (`vX.Y.Z`), move `## [Unreleased]` items into `## [vX.Y.Z] - YYYY-MM-DD`, leave an empty `## [Unreleased]` heading above it, keep `docs/FEATURES.md` aligned, and ask the user whether they also want to: (1) commit the release docs, (2) create a Git tag (`vX.Y.Z`), and (3) push the commit/tag to remote.

## 4. Mandatory Pre-Completion Self-Check & Guardrails

- **Pre-Completion Check**: Before finishing any turn where you created, edited, renamed, or deleted non-documentation files, verify with `git status --short` that `CHANGELOG.md` (and `docs/FEATURES.md` / `PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` when applicable) were updated in the same turn. Do not conclude until those updates are written.
- **Verify Every Fact**: Document only files, symbols, behaviors, and outputs directly observed in the repository. Never copy secrets or `.env` values.
- **Skip Doc-Only & Read-Only Turns**: Do not add `CHANGELOG.md` churn for read-only Q&A turns or purely editorial documentation updates (such as fixing typos in `README.md` or running doc syncs).
